mctx is a lightweight terminal notepad for the .mctx memory context format
used by AI agents as persistent memory.

It presents a two-panel editor: the section list from the file's %%INDEX
block on the left (name, durability tier, version), and a body editor on the
right. Saving a section bumps its v: counter and rebuilds the byte-offset
index so readers can seek straight to a section without scanning the file.

Also ships the zero-dependency mctx Rust library (src/mctx.rs) for reading
and writing .mctx files programmatically.

WWW: https://github.com/cyberhatc/mctx
